- Intro (world.js `playIntro`, ~7s, 1.6x on repeat visits via sessionStorage `fy-intro`, any key/tap speeds it up): CSS star twinkles with a load ring, crouches and launches up the 8° lean, cover fades onto a night island, `--dawn` lifts the sky and lights, 3D star falls from just above the screen, impact (flash, shockwaves, debris, shake), robot pops out with a spin-jump and hero pose, then the HUD, name plates and help card arrive. Header stays hidden (`html.world-intro .hud`) until landing unless focused.
- Island: `world-map.js` (pure layout, previewed by `.impeccable/tools/map-preview.html`): u = screen right, v = toward camera, `toXZ/toUV`; terraced regions (beach .5, low 3, mid 5.6, top 8.2), stairs, decks (dock, pier, bridge, shrine dais), river, paths, `spots` (landing by the dock, camp, games plaza, shrine...). `world-island.js` `buildIsland`: terrain mesh + rock-column cliffs + props baked into vertex-coloured meshes, water/stream/waterfall shaders, wind grass that parts around Niko, `nav` walk grid + A* (stairs skip the cliff-foot test and allow 0.65 steps), `occlude` (dither scenery in front of Niko), `atmos` (cloud shadows drifting + cool haze near sea level; apply to every lit static material). Zones: shrine + lectern (Resume) at the back, plateau camp (tent About + Skills facing a campfire clearing), ruins stairs + Career stones, cliffside plaza with the 6 game monoliths in a back arc facing its centre, beach/dock start (Contact mailbox on the pier).
- Look (user wanted Genshin/BotW feel, not flat): sun from screen upper-left `(-25,30,11)` so shadows fall toward the viewer (a sun behind the camera hid every shadow), warm sun / cool hemi / cool fill, toon ramp `[74,92,186,236,255]`, baked occlusion (`gradeY` on columns/trees, cliff-foot AO + sunlit lips + meadow patches in `groundColour`), CSS grade on `.world-vignette::before/::after` (soft-light sun bloom, faint shafts, cool bottom haze, × `--dawn`). Camera: old look restored, offset (40, 58, 40) so the view looks straight at Niko at ~45.7° down (he sits in the centre). Pitch is live: `debug.angle(degrees)` or `?angle=` (clamped 10–80), and the camera stays on that sphere. Right-drag orbits yaw (0.12°/px, damp 14). Mouse shifts the frame (35%×2 across, 25%×2 up, damp 15). Follow damp 6–18 with speed. Default yaw is the old diagonal. Middle-click or G locks the training dummy on the spawn court: Niko turns toward it at 720°/s (written on the yaw, a quaternion copy folds past ±90°) and the four run lock-on clips play in that facing (forward, back, left, right). A diagonal blends the two neighbouring run clips, except back-left and back-right, which ease onto `runB` with the hips yawed onto that diagonal and the chest yawed back toward the target. The file's left and right strafes face the other way, so a left move plays the clip labeled right. Lock idle is `assets/niko/Idle.fbx`. Standing still pitches the chest and head up toward the camera (world pitch around his right; the old local rotateX pointed the Mixamo bones the wrong way). The walk quaternion set stays at weight 0. Lock hip curves are scaled ×100 onto the centimeter Mixamo skeleton so the bob stays a bob. A lock-on key press plays the run clip, starting at the frame closest to the current arms. The facing turns on a circle, and a fast left-right swap jumps the aim and crossfades the two run clips instead of dipping through idle. Unity arm curves (shoulders, arms, hands) are stored as (x, -y, -z, w) relative to the FBX, so those two signs are flipped before retarget or each wrist crosses to the other side. Letting go blends the arms back on the short arc. The camera yaw eases behind him (damp 10) and the frame sits halfway between them. Once the yaw is within 18°, either of them leaving the padded screen (or 18 units apart) drops the lock after 0.2 s. Mouse look while locked is clamped so it cannot push them off screen. Intro: Rigel lands on the beach (`landing`) and Niko spawns there; shrine star + beam appear after.
- Sharp look (user: colours looked washed/blurry): `makeRamp()` = 3 crisp toon bands shared by island + world.js props (Niko keeps his own ramp), rim 0.06, sun 3.35 / hemi 0.85, shadow radius 1.5, smaller CSS bloom. `groundColour` uses hard `cut()` thresholds (Pixel_Pass-style albedo patches: `grassSun`/`grassShade`/`grassDeep` from separate noises, crisp paths/tide line/camp, 2-step cliff AO) and is baked into a 400² ground texture (`groundTexture`, terrain uv = world xz) plus `grassMask`; `groundAt(x,z)` samples both. Greens are saturated toward Pixel_Pass albedo #71A200.
- Look decision (users preferred the GitHub colours): keep the 3-band `makeRamp` [100,176,255], dark ungraded shadows, hard `cut()` patches, 2-step cliff AO, Niko on his own ramp + lavender rim. Rejected: a 2-tone cel ramp + shade/sun colour grade (too flat, shadows too light). Post edge/outline pass in world.js `post` is opt-in (`?fx=1`, `?pixel=3`), off by default. Soft shapes kept: `G.box`/slab = RoundedBox, rocks/blobs = smooth `boulder`, cliff columns smooth, logs/barrels round; world.js `box()` always rounds.
- Space + wind: `MAP.K = 1.32` spreads authored uv (`MAP.lay(u,v)`; stops/placeUV use it; widths unscaled), GRID ±44, ground TEX 640. Wind = `WIND_GLSL` `windGust` gust bands rolling along `WIND_DIR` + small base lean, crown roll wave, gentle `aLeaf` (size, phase) flutter; all on `windTime` = climate's integrated wind phase (~1.2/s fair), so strength changes never jump. The Pixelage-demo `windField` (-1..1 sway, ×3.2 lean, leaf shear, 46° grass) was tried and REJECTED as ugly/over-bent: keep bends small. Trunk sway weight stays 0. No grass on the beach.
- Assets (after `sampleModels/stylized_bush.glb` + `stylized_low-poly_stone.glb`): rocks = `chisel()` (icosphere pulled onto random planes with `softMin` = flat faces, soft bevels), `G.stones` clusters for big scatter/sea rocks, cliffs = `basalt()` columns. `sized(geo, build)` pieces are rebuilt at real size in `makeBake.add` so bevels never stretch (box, slab, columns). Stairs = stacked slabs + cheek blocks (no sloped curbs). Shadow grain fix: world.js patches PCF `phi` to a constant. Foliage (bush, round tree, pine share it; Niko-scaled): dark `coreBall` core + `leafBall` shell of alpha-tested cards from `foliageTexture()` atlas (tile 0 = small rounded leaf cluster, tile 1 = needle spray), ellipsoid normals, `swayPair` shared sway box, `plant()` puts core in `bake` and cards in `leafBake` (`leafMaterial` + `leafDepth` for shadows). Atlas has 3 tiles (bush sprig 0, needles 1, `TWIG_TILE` 2 = tiny tree leaves; user wanted tree leaves small). Bush card .26, s .95–1.35 (knee–hip); tree card .3 on the twig tile; pine card .6. world-check walk waits 120 s.
- Effects (ref bruno-simon.com): post always renders to a half-float target; dual-filter bloom (`post` bloom, `?bloom=0`, `debug.post({bloom,threshold,knee,strength})`; user found bloom bled colour: now threshold 1.22 / knee .12 / strength .2 in sRGB units (≈ linear 1.6, only glow() light sources), the intro impact flash sprite was removed (impactLight 35). `THREE.ShaderChunk.colorspace_fragment` is patched to always sRGB-encode (max(rgb,0) first, NaN guard), also into the post target, and the composite does no conversion: linear-space MSAA/blending had made grass and shade paler whenever bloom was on, so bloom on/off now look the same apart from the glow (check: `glow-parts.mjs`, `launch-shots.mjs`); adaptQuality drops DPR to 1, then bloom, then .75). Light sources are HDR: `glow(color, power)`, island `glowing` ×2.4, fire ×2.2. Lamp light: `lampLights` uniform (24 spheres, lanterns + campfire, flicker in `update`) added in `atmos` and `lamped()` (world.js toon/painted/lining, so Niko too). Wind lines = `world-wind.js` (screen-width ribbons, draw-in/loop/wipe, spawn on a random screen point; DoubleSide or they get culled). Tree sway follows the same gust bands (lean capped at 1.05× the baked weight); a fast shake still reads as "someone hitting the tree", so the motion is a traveling wave, not a vibration. Grass trampling: `trail` RT ping-pong (rg lean×amount, b amount; soft 0.58 stamp, decay ~0.7/s ≈3 s). Standing = flatten only (no radial crater; tips scatter toward camera); walking = lean along the step. Grass shader: mild screen roll, height squash, world tipPush, wind ×(1−0.92·press). Check: `trail-shot.mjs`. Loop dt is clamped ≥ 0 (settle made it negative). Tools: `trail-shot.mjs`, `wind-peek.mjs`, island-shots env `JS`.
- Controls: floating touch stick in world.js (`stick`, `.world-stick`; a touch that drags > 12 px becomes the stick where the drag began, base stays fixed, knob clamps at the 46 px rim, light push = slower walk via `state.pace`, which also scales the run clip); a short tap/click still walks. Zoom: wheel + two-finger pinch (`touches`, `pinch`) feed `zoomBy` → `zoomGoal`, eased in `easeZoom` (play 0.7–1.7; intro tweens camera.zoom directly). `debug.zoom(z)` is the only way past that: down to 0.25 to see more of Niko, and the wheel keeps 0.25–8 until `debug.zoom(null)`. `zoom-check.mjs` tests wheel, pinch, fixed stick.
- Perf (measured with `perf-check.mjs [base] [dpr] [cpuThrottle]`, headful real GPU, env SHORT/Q): the offscreen HDR target + MSAA resolve cost 2–4x the scene itself; grass/leaves/props each only ~5 ms at 3x. So: `lite` (coarse, or `?lite=1`; `?lite=0` opts out) renders straight to the screen (no post), DPR cap 2 everywhere (`MAX_RATIO`), island `halos` (additive sprites on lanterns/fire + shrine inlay disc) show whenever bloom is off; offscreen MSAA only below 1.5x DPR (`?msaa=1/0`); depth texture only with `?fx=1`. adaptQuality (real frame time, hitches capped at 250 ms) ladder: MSAA off → bloom off → DPR −0.25 down to 1, then only while still > 34 ms down to `MIN_RATIO` 0.6 (climbs back toward 1 under 14 ms); > 60 ms takes all steps at once. Software GL (SwiftShader/llvmpipe/Basic Render) → lite at 0.75x + console warning; `?diag=1` shows it. Oct 2026 perf pass (desktop AMD iGPU, bare scene 31.9 → 22.7 ms): it is per-pixel bound (GPU timer queries under-report on ANGLE; CPU time in uniform*() is GPU back-pressure). Props/leaves/grass are merged per `CULL_CELL` 12-unit square (`bake.build(mat, { cell, reach })`, grass one InstancedMesh per square with its own boundingSphere) so camera + shadow camera cull and near squares draw first; cloud noise is drawn once per frame into `makeCloudMap` (512², r+g/255 packed) and `cloudAt` reads it (rays' `beamAt` still uses `CLOUD_NOISE_GLSL`); lamps culled to the view and packed first (`lampCount`); shadow 5×5 tent probes its 9 even taps first and only edges take all 25. Sun shadow map (4096, redrawn every frame for Niko + sway) ≈ 15% of the bare scene. Tools: `perf-compare.mjs <urlA> <urlB>` (alternating medians; serve an old build from a `git worktree` with its OWN serve.mjs on another port), `perf-ab.mjs` (A/B toggles, `SOFT=1` SwiftShader for steady ranking), `gpu-profile.mjs`, `cpu-profile.mjs`, `perf-desk.mjs`, `adapt-watch.mjs`, `look-check.mjs` (overcast/fair/night/zoomout shots). Renderer has `stencil: true` (eye mask on the screen path). Prewarm compiles programs for both the target and the screen. Load fallbacks: textures 15 s, Niko 25 s (both still prewarm), hard reveal 40 s. Lite at 2x on a phone viewport: 25.5 → 9.2 ms; 15.8 ms with 4x CPU throttle.
- Mobile render fixes: shrine beam went black on portrait (MSAA samples varyings past the edge, `pow(negative)` = NaN on D3D, bloom smeared it into blocks). Rule: clamp every shader `pow` base; bloom `shrink` drops NaN/Inf taps. No half-float support → 8-bit targets, bloom keys on the min channel × gain (`?hdr=0` to test). Phones drop to 0.75x DPR before losing bloom. `?diag=1` overlay (ms, dpr, bloom, hdr, reduced motion, GPU). Repro on the real GPU: `shrine-black.mjs [base] [prefix] 1` (headful Edge; swiftshader hides it); debug `scene()/island()/shrineStar()`. Tap/click routes draw dotted `routeDots` (InstancedMesh, `showRoute`/`updateRoute`, dots draw out from Niko and are eaten as he passes). Fixed: `.world-sky::before` (z-index 1) sat over the canvas and ate every click; `.world-sky` now `isolation: isolate; pointer-events: none`. Check: `touch-check.mjs [base] [prefix]` (390×844 touch).
- Grass = Pixel_Pass port (ref copy in `.impeccable/ref-pixelpass/`): one InstancedMesh of camera-facing leaf cards on a jittered grid (0.21 spacing, 0.3 coarse) wherever `grassMask`, painted the ground colour at the base, up normal + `transformed = 0` after projection so light/shadow/cloud come from the base, procedural blade masks (`leafMask`), wind = `windGust` lean + flutter (≤38° bend), Niko tramples via the `trail` map; 1.2% accent cards; dune cards on the beach.
