- In-game body is `assets/niko/low-poly-humanoid-v6-clean.glb` (Tripo low-poly humanoid, base-color texture, yaw −90° so he faces +Z), made from the user's `-v6.glb` (Blender face edit; mesh-clean also drops Blender's duplicate unused armature/skin, which would steal the animation binding) by `python tex-pad.py <in.glb> ../review/<x>.jpg` (pads atlas islands over the black gaps so seams/mips don't go dark) then `node mesh-clean.mjs <in> <out> --texture ../review/<x>.jpg` (collapses folded slivers, fills small holes, drops degenerate tris, smooth normals shared across UV seams; UVs/skin untouched). Check any body with `python mesh-audit.py <glb> [yMin]`. Hair is `assets/niko/hair-short.glb` (Sketchfab cap): world matrix baked, yawed onto the nose, scaled to 1.28× the skull width. `HAIR_FIT { scale: 1, x: 0.01, y: -0.02, z: 0.01 }` (live `debug.hair({scale, x, y, z})`: x toward the nose, y up, z toward his right). The hair outline is its own thin hull: only faces pointing away from the skull, pushed straight out from it, so the body's ink doesn't fill the gaps between spikes., then baked into Head-local space and parented to the Head bone (`seatHair` in `useNikoModel`) so it follows idle, run, and the face-up look. It keeps the file's pale material and the body toon. Painted eyes from `assets/niko-eyes.png` are the head's own front triangles (`paintEyes`, skinned with the face) so they stay on the mesh from the side. Eyes are lit by the skin's toon chain (`eyeMaterial(..., { lit })`, receive shadows). Placement = `EYE_FIT { gap, width, height, raise }` in reference px (live: `debug.eyes({...})`, `face-fit.mjs` env `EYES='{"gap":28}'`), over `FACE_REF` (crown/nose rows on the user's front T-pose reference) × `faceAnchor` (mesh nose tip = sharpest forward spike on the centre profile; crown-to-nose sets the scale) × `paintBox` (sclera+lash alpha bounds inside each atlas tile). Review: `face-fit.mjs [base] [prefix]` (front/side via `debug.faceView(angle)`, plus the game view; logs the anchor). Idle and run are not procedural: `assets/niko/Idle.fbx` and `assets/Running (1).fbx` are retargeted at load in `useNikoModel` by Mixamo bone name (`mixamorig` stripped), so a new Mixamo body uses the same files. Niko is now the Tripo model (ref `Low-Poly Starry Mage Explorer.png`/`.glb` in repo root), The game wears separate skinned pieces `assets/niko/{body,hair,coat,clothes,shoes}.glb` on one skeleton (`bot.parts`; esbuild binary loader, so `file://` works). Pipeline in `.impeccable/tools` (run from there): `niko-clean.mjs` → `niko-split.mjs` → `niko-rig.mjs` writes `assets/niko.glb`, then `niko-parts.mjs` splits it. `niko-body-blend.py` (Blender) rebuilds `body.glb` and `body-clean.blend` from `body-source.glb` into one connected bald T-pose. `niko-tpose-rig.py` fits Y Bot's Mixamo skeleton onto `niko-t-pose.glb` (that source stays untouched) and writes `niko-t-pose-rigged.glb`: welds split corners, smooths normals, one subdivision (~7.7k verts) after the joints are placed, then skins. `niko-tpose-clips.mjs` adds idle/walk/run; re-running the rigger wipes those clips, so rebake and rebuild the bundle. That file is the clean body slot. Its origin is the soles; the game plants that box on the ground (the old 0.5×scale waist lift is not applied). Eyes are the painted atlas decals, raycast onto the face and parented to Head. Hair, coat, clothes, and shoes stay separate GLBs on this skeleton; the older outfit files are still skinned to the previous rig. `niko-rig.mjs` still builds the master rig: face carve (face texture = blush/nose/mouth only), bang "eye windows" cut + plates, `eyeL`/`eyeR` decal meshes (own 0..1 UVs, ray-cast in front of the skin), hands = palm + 5 fingers × 3 segments (rest dirs match Mixamo: fingers +x, thumb (.77,-.45,.45)), standard Mixamo skeleton with unprefixed names (Hips…Spine2, Left/RightShoulder/Arm/ForeArm/Hand + all finger bones, UpLeg/Leg/Foot/ToeBase) + Hair/Ahoge/Lantern + `Cape{c}_{k}` 7×5 spring chains, socket nodes `LeftHandSocket`/`RightHandSocket`/`HeadSocket`/`BackSocket`.
- Animations: manifest `.impeccable/anim/clips.json` (name → `{file, clip?}`, FBX or GLB, any Mixamo T-pose rig). `node niko-anim.mjs` (server on :8765) dumps each via `anim-dump.html` to `anim/<name>.json` (world rotations relative to the source rest + hips + restPositions), then `niko-rig.mjs` retargets by bone name (missing bones follow parent). idle/walk = Xbot.glb, run = `Running.fbx` (fists curl). To add one: add the line, run niko-anim then niko-rig.
